= Multi-agent system — Simple =

A '''multi-agent system''' is a computer system with several agents that interact.

The agents may:

* work together;
* compete;
* divide tasks;
* communicate;
* negotiate;
* make separate decisions.

Multi-agent systems existed long before modern large language models.

A group of LLM-based agents can be a multi-agent system, but using the same model several times does not automatically create one.

